course: dictionary
lesson: 13345
title: Hairball, from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context is the words and sentences around a word, and they often leave clues to its meaning. «After Whiskers licked her fur, she coughed up a furry hairball on the rug.» Coughing and licking point to a cat, so a hairball must come from inside a cat.
explain: Hairball also has a second, informal meaning. «Dad pulled a big hairball out of the bathroom plughole.» Nobody coughed it up here, so it cannot be a cat's hairball. It is a tangle of hair that has blocked the plughole.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try «a tangle of hair» in the plughole sentence: it still makes sense. Try «a cat's stomach ball» there, and it does not. The sentence tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A hairball is a ball of hair that forms in an animal's stomach, especially a cat's.
fact: Cats swallow fur when they lick themselves clean.
fact: A cat may then cough the hairball up.
fact: Brushing a cat helps prevent hairballs.
fact: Informally, a hairball can also be a tangle of hair in a hairbrush or plughole.
exercise: «After Whiskers licked her fur, she coughed up a hairball.» What is a hairball here? | *A ball of hair that a cat has swallowed and coughed up | A toy made of wool | A type of cat food | A ball of hair from a cat's stomach, coughed up
exercise: «Dad pulled a hairball out of the bathroom plughole.» What does hairball mean here? | A soft, fluffy towel | *A tangle of hair blocking a drain | A cat's stomach ball | A bathroom tile
exercise: «Brushing your cat each day helps stop hairballs.» What does brushing help prevent? | *Hairballs forming in a cat's stomach | Cats being noisy | A cat getting wet | A cat losing its toys
test: «Mum found a hairball in the hairbrush and threw it away.» What does hairball mean? | *A tangle of hair in the brush | A small toy | A cat's stomach ball | A bird's nest
test: «The cat coughed, and a hairball landed on the carpet.» Which words are the clues that help you work out the meaning? | *coughed and landed on the carpet | hairball and landed | the and a | cat and the
exam: «The vet said Pepper had too many hairballs, so she gave advice on brushing.» What does the word hairballs most likely mean here? | Lumps of hair that form in a cat's stomach and are coughed up | *Lumps of hair that form in a cat's stomach and are coughed up, which the vet is worried about | Pieces of cat food | Bits of string from the garden
